WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.460
In 1945, Korea became an almost perfect scientific experiment:

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.560
one population with the same geography and culture

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.880
became two separate test groups: one capitalist, and one very not.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.780
FIGHT!

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.940
No matter what metric you use: GDP, 
 population, life expectancy, education,

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.910
technology, military, really

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.080
whatever, we can now declare South Korea the winner.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.260
The North is so underdeveloped that glancing at a nighttime

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.140
aerial photo might fool you into thinking it's the Pacific

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:37.740
Ocean. All of this makes it tempting to see as a failed state and even easier to laugh when it threatens

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.900
militaries much stronger than its own.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.980
But compare the country not to what it could be, but to what it should be.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.440
With the GDP of an African country you've never heard of and 30 percent of its population

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:57.030
undernourished, the North should be erupting in revolution. Even setting aside internal conflict, North Korea acts like a younger sibling,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:04.580
provoking his much stronger brothers, except the threat is nuclear war, and all with the military might of tiny Belgium.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.140
If Kim Jong-Un is just a crazy mad man, he's been

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.140
incredibly lucky to survive all of this. Nobody rolls that many natural twenties. Life has never been better for the Kim family:

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.540
his people may be starving and his diplomacy hostile, but he lives in perpetual

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.869
We Love the King Day. This makes him not a *good* leader,

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:32.758
but a good *leader*, a master of politics who stays in power despite everyone working against him. So, just how does he do it?

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:46.540
Even the most brutal dictator prioritizes the needs of his citizens, knowing that a hungry or unhappy population is a ticking time bomb,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.620
counting down to the beheading of its leader.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:55.780
But North Korea is a rare exception. As hungry as you may be, you've been taught that it's no different anywhere else;

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.940
revolting would do no good, biting the only hand that even

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.620
occasionally feeds you. Low quality of life is not just the unfortunate consequence of misaligned priorities, it's also a

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:14.119
beneficial political decision: no one will demand freedom of speech when they're barely able to feed their family. People are far too

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.369
preoccupied with the latter. Besides, Kim will make personally sure the food doesn't go wasted.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:27.350
You may hear of coming reform, but it's almost always wishful thinking. Kim knows that a better life would create far too ambitious a

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:33.320
population. What would normally be incompetence is actually political strategy in the case of North Korea.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.650
Countries may claim only to war in the name of freedom and democracy,

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.560
but it's usually far more complex than that.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:51.199
Offensive wars are fought when the inconvenience of a problem outweighs the cost of war.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:58.639
North Korea knows that it can provoke as much as it wants, so long as it doesn't cross that threshold. And provoke it does:

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.609
Kim has shot South Korean soldiers, sunk

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:07.819
submarines, broken a nuclear weapons agreement and fired missiles into not-so-nice places. These make the news,

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:15.080
scaring the world into thinking that war is coming. The media is happy to suggest that this time, Kim really is getting serious.

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:18.859
When people are sufficiently scared, Kim opens negotiations:

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:21.649
"Send us some food aid, and we promise to chill."

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:27.440
Smart politicians know how hollow these threats are but they too are playing the political game.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.600
Nobody who wants to be reelected will ignore what their constituents perceive to be a threat to national

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.040
security, but there is a popular alternative:

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:42.680
getting tough with sanctions. If a country isn't playing nice, you raise the prices of its goods to anger its

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.529
population. This puts pressure on the government, who must behave or risk revolution.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:55.329
North Koreans, however, are unlikely to turn on their glorious Leader, and any sanctions big enough to actually make a difference would be blocked by

00:03:55.329 --> 00:04:01.449
China, who would like to avoid 25 million unskilled workers entering its borders and the biggest military in the world

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:08.679
looking over its shoulder. The political mood swings from hard to soft to hard again after each policy fails.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.340
Playing soft only helps Kim and getting tough has little effect

00:04:12.889 --> 00:04:15.789
America took a break called Strategic Patience,

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:21.729
but we quickly learned exactly what that really means. Still, Kim knows this can't go on forever.

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:30.099
Eventually someone is going to get impatient, and when that happens, things don't look good for an army of biplanes, even if they are

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.100
camouflaged. So Kim plays the ultimate bomb card.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.400
These aren't the signs of some crazy ambition to conquer the world.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.829
They're a strategic necessity.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.900
A chess player is made good by anticipating his opponent's next move.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.520
You're never going to beat a much better player, because he can figure out both his next best move and

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.340
yours too, but if you know you're the weaker player,

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:09.060
you can stop trying to beat him by skill and change strategies. By sometimes making irrational

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:14.880
unexplainable moves, your opponent loses that advantage. North Korea does exactly this.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:21.639
No military, no matter how much stronger it may be, wants to risk finding a loose cannon with nuclear weapons,

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.800
and Kim knows this. When you hear stories about Kim killing his own family with anti-aircraft

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.270
guns, pay attention to what that makes you think about him and then consider

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:36.340
how that actually plays to his advantage. Kim knows that he can't out-gun America,

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.929
but he can lessen their power by being too unpredictable to mess with.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:47.739
As long as you keep hearing news of missile tests, impending war, and famine, you can be sure Kim is thriving.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:52.720
His country may be a failure, but his rule is anything but.

